// Per-tick performance ceilings for `simrunner bench`, checked by
// `scripts/check-perf.sh`.
//
// WHAT THESE ARE
//
// Cliff detectors: an accidentally quadratic loop, a per-tick allocation that
// was not there yesterday, a linear scan that became a scan over every
// entity. They sit at roughly three times the p99 a developer machine
// produces, because a shared CI runner is slower and noisier and a tighter
// gate fails on neighbours rather than on regressions.
//
// Measured variance on a developer machine across three runs of three
// repeats: p99 spread was 1.1x-1.2x. CI will be worse.
//
// HOW THESE RELATE TO docs/04 §12
//
// §12 budgets 6 ms of a 50 ms tick for pathfinding at 200 population and
// 400 entities. `marching-8p` — eight players keeping 40 mobile units each
// in the field, so ~320 units under way at once, with no combat and no AI —
// spent about 6.5 ms at p99 on per-unit A* at the end of M3, nearly all of
// it planning paths. The sector graph and flow fields of M4 chunk 1 brought
// that to about 2.4 ms (and `crowded` from 2.9 ms to 1.9 ms), measured on
// the same developer machine; the ceilings below were lowered to three
// times the new numbers in the same commit.
//
// The scenario is deliberately unkind to flow fields: each order picks a
// random handful of a player's units, scattered across the map by earlier
// orders, so a group spans about ten sectors and its corridor is wide. Real
// groups are clustered and their fields are narrower.
//
// The ceilings below are still deliberately loose. The useful signal is the
// trend, printed on every run. When a system lands that makes a scenario
// meaningfully slower, lower the ceiling to three times the new number in
// the same commit — a ceiling that is never revisited stops being a gate.
//
// Verify §12 properly on known hardware at milestone review. A shared runner
// cannot answer that question and should not pretend to.
(
    scenarios: [
        (
            name: "economy-2p",
            note: "a settled two-player economy: gathering, drop-off, building",
            max_p99_us: 350.0,
        ),
        (
            name: "marching-8p",
            note: "eight players pathing ~320 units at once; the docs/04 §5 load",
            max_p99_us: 7500.0,
        ),
        (
            name: "crowded",
            note: "economy and marching together on a large map",
            max_p99_us: 6000.0,
        ),
    ],
)
